  "bucket_2_4_resolution_status": {
    "decision_a_c1_c2_exact_overlap": "RESOLVED 2026-10-14 (see c1_cross_pool_fix_report.json) -- 8 sequences removed from C1 (kept in C2, per approved 'preserve C2's biological-annotation precedence'), replaced 1:1 from the UniProtKB candidate universe, screened against FR1 positives, 179 conflicts, C2, and C3. Canonical C1 artifact is now stage_c1_decoys_v3.fasta.",
    "decision_b_c2_homology_to_e1_positive": "RESOLVED 2026-10-14 (see c2_cross_pool_fix_report.json) -- C2-EFDBC5460B ('LYQEPVLGPVRGPFP') excluded as a conservative leakage-risk decision (NOT claimed experimentally inactive), replaced 1:1 from the experimentally-reported Peptipedia tier, screened against FR1 positives, 179 conflicts, remaining C2, C1 v3, and C3. Canonical C2 artifact is now stage_c2_bioactive_unlabeled_v2.fasta.",
    "additional_homology_candidates": "Of the 14 other candidates found alongside the project-owner-flagged C2/FR1-positive pair, reviewed individually (not auto-excluded by cluster membership): 3 were fully resolved as a side effect of Decision A (their shared member was one of the 8 exact C1/C2 duplicates, now removed from C1); 11 remain as near-duplicate (not exact) C1<->C2 pairs post-fix. All are C1<->C2 only (no FR1-positive involvement) and from peptide families with no plausible antioxidant mechanism (ribosomal/zinc-ribbon proteins, protamine-like and homeodomain cell-penetrating peptides, actin/gliadin fragments, cysteine-rich defensin-like peptides) -- assessed as redundant construction overlap between two unlabeled pools, not a label-leakage risk, since neither pool carries ground truth. Recommendation: accept and document as a known, bounded limitation (same treatment as C1's intentional record-level duplicates) rather than a further exclude-and-replace cycle. See audit_cross_pool_homology_clusters.csv for the full per-cluster evidence; revisit if the project owner wants a stricter policy."
  },
